Executive Council Resolution No. (14) of 2026 Approving the Activities Related to the Use of Autonomous Vehicles and their Operational Phases in the Emirate of Dubai
Article (7): Using Autonomous Vehicles for Personal Purposes
a. An individual who owns an Autonomous Vehicle intended for personal use must not activate the Autonomous Driving System except during the Third Phase of the operation of Autonomous Vehicles, and only after obtaining the relevant approval of the RTA.
b. An Autonomous Vehicle may only be used in accordance with paragraph (a) of this Article if, at the time of its initial registration in the Emirate, the Vehicle was supplied by the approved local Agent for that specific type of Vehicle.
c. Where the RTA approves the activation of the Autonomous Driving System, the owner of the Autonomous Vehicle must:
1. activate the Autonomous Driving System in coordination with, or under the direct supervision of the Agent;
2. use the Autonomous Vehicle on the Roads and lanes, and in the areas, specified by the RTA;
3. where a child is on board, ensure that the child is accompanied by another person, subject to the age requirements prescribed for the child and the accompanying person by resolution of the Director General;
4. comply with the safety requirements and standards approved by the RTA for the use of Autonomous Vehicles;

Law No. (9) of 2023 Regulating the Operation of Autonomous Vehicles in the Emirate of Dubai
Article (8): Requirements for Licensing Autonomous Vehicles
To be licensed, an Autonomous Vehicle must:
1. be sourced from the authorised local Agent for that type of Autonomous Vehicles in the Emirate, at the time of initial registration;
2. be registered in its source country or country of origin, and have a proven record of use on the public Roads designated for its category and type in that country;
3. pass the technical inspection prescribed by the RTA;
4. be equipped to read and respond to Traffic Signs, and capable of responding to Road priorities and travelling on Roads;
5. meet the security and safety standards and specifications, and be equipped with the systems required to interact with Roads and their users in accordance with the relevant guidelines adopted by the RTA;
6. conform to the specifications approved in the UAE;
7. be insured with an insurance company licensed to operate in the UAE, as prescribed by the Director General in this respect; and 8. meet any other conditions determined pursuant to the relevant resolutions issued by the Director General.

Executive Council Resolution No. (14) of 2026 Approving the Activities Related to the Use of Autonomous Vehicles and their Operational Phases in the Emirate of Dubai
Article (6): Obligations of Operators during the Third Phase
During the Third Phase of the operation of Autonomous Vehicles, an Operator must:
1. not operate Autonomous Vehicles without first obtaining the relevant Permit;
2. comply with the operational standards and performance and safety indicators specified by the RTA for Autonomous Vehicles;
3. provide the RTA with an undertaking that Autonomous Vehicles will not obstruct traffic or compromise the safety of Road Users during its operation;
4. provide the RTA and the Competent Entities in the Emirate, upon request, with the necessary data and information related to the operation of Autonomous Vehicles; and 5. fulfil any other obligations determined pursuant to the relevant resolution of the Director General.

